<h3>2026-08-26 — Documentation System Standard as in-app definition</h3>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>What.</strong> Defined the one documentation system in <code>STANDARD.tt</code>: human navigation (home / module index / page chrome), docs-must-match-code, and a full SQL cutover that deletes every DocumentationConfig JSON file. Linked from DocumentationMasterPlan.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Why.</strong> STANDARD.md already said SQL is the catalog, but JSON is still live, humans cannot navigate 600 pages, and docs drift from code. The user asked for one system that is human-readable, human-navigable, current with the code, and free of the JSON catalog.</p>
<p class="doc-body"><strong>Files.</strong> <code>Comserv/root/Documentation/STANDARD.tt</code>, <code>Comserv/root/Documentation/DocumentationMasterPlan.tt</code></p>
</div>
